Parity decisions (honest, no scope narrowing):
  • Reuses the shared `useLiveConnection` value types LiveConnectionStatus / LiveConnectionSnapshot /
    LiveConnectionReading / LiveConnectionTransport (public, defined in LiveIndicator.Projection.swift —
    the same module; cannot redefine without a duplicate-symbol clash). Everything else is owned by this
    surface with the `LiveTelemetrySegment` prefix.
  • The web segment renders exactly ONE of four statuses — there is no skeleton/spinner-only gate in the
    source. The P4 leaf states map onto the web's real surfaces (documented in the Projection header):
      loading/initial → unknown ("Idle", muted) ·  empty(no lastMessage) → chip with NO age stamp
      error/offline   → disconnected ("Offline") ·  stale → connected with the freshness stamp aging
    No chrome was invented that the web source does not have, and no web surface was dropped.
  • i18n: all 11 keys resolve through NSLocalizedString (table "LiveTelemetrySegment"); the four web
    `t('statusBar.live.*')` labels (note "Idle" for unknown, the web divergence from LiveIndicator's
    "Unknown"), the tooltip title + "Last message {{age}} ago", the aria label, the three compact age
    unit forms ({{count}}s/m/h — the web ageSecondsLabel hard-codes these inline), and the native link
    hint. No English/bare literals in Swift.
  • Navigation: the web `<Link to="/signal-diff">` becomes an injected onOpen closure; the default
    broadcasts LiveTelemetrySegmentMeta.openLiveExplorerNotification carrying route "/signal-diff" so the
    host shell routes without the surface owning the router (VersionSegment NotificationCenter precedent).
  • Tokens (P1/S9): Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing only. Tooltip = native `.help()` (web <Tooltip>).
    Telemetry (P1/S11): view.opened emitted exactly once on first appear. A11y: single labelled element,
    Reduce-Motion-gated spinner, decorative dot/icon hidden, open hint.

